<title>AUSTRALIA: RTRS-Top 20 Australian Dividend Yields - Nov 4.</title>
<headline>RTRS-Top 20 Australian Dividend Yields - Nov 4.</headline>
<dateline>SYDNEY 1996-11-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>Twenty highest dividend yields for Australian companies included in the 320-share All Ordinaries Index based on closing prices on Friday.</p>
<p>Dividends based on rolling 12 months.</p>
<p>Yields are not grossed up for franking credits.</p>
<p>				Dividend</p>
<p>Rank Name		    Yield    Close</p>
<p> 1   Villa World	    10.78    1.02</p>
<p> 2   Prime Credit Tr	10.32    0.95</p>
<p> 3   Prop Income Inv	10.06    1.01</p>
<p> 4   McIntosh Sec	    9.78    0.92</p>
<p> 5   Indu Property	   9.48    0.96</p>
<p> 6   BT Prop Trust	   9.43    1.73</p>
<p> 7   Colonial Mutual	 9.29    1.12</p>
<p> 8   MT Leyshon Gold	 9.26    2.70</p>
<p> 9   Aust Tour		 9.15    0.82</p>
<p>10   Armstrong Retail	8.80    0.75</p>
<p>11   Centro Prop	     8.74    2.23</p>
<p>12   Gandel Retail Tr	8.67    0.90</p>
<p>13   Equitilink		8.47    0.59</p>
<p>14   Gen Prop Tr	     8.45    2.38</p>
<p>15   Central Equity	  8.41    1.07</p>
<p>16   Advance Pro CB	  8.35    1.39</p>
<p>17   Barclays Mirvac	 8.33    1.32</p>
<p>18   Capcount Prop	   8.19    0.83</p>
<p>19   Natl In Prop	    8.12    1.03</p>
<p>20   Westfield Trust	 8.12    2.39</p>
<p>-- Sydney Newsroom 61-2 373-1800</p>
